===== Available Tools =====
- ToolName: list_schemas             Description: List all schemas in the database
- ToolName: list_objects             Description: List objects in a schema
- ToolName: get_object_details       Description: Show detailed information about a database object
- ToolName: explain_query            Description: Explains the execution plan for a SQL query, showing how the database will execute it and provides detailed cost estimates.
- ToolName: analyze_workload_indexes Description: Analyze frequently executed queries in the database and recommend optimal indexes
- ToolName: analyze_query_indexes    Description: Analyze a list of (up to 10) SQL queries and recommend optimal indexes
- ToolName: analyze_db_health        Description: Analyzes database health. Here are the available health checks:
- index - checks for invalid, duplicate, and bloated indexes
- connection - checks the number of connection and their utilization
- vacuum - checks vacuum health for transaction id wraparound
- sequence - checks sequences at risk of exceeding their maximum value
- replication - checks replication health including lag and slots
- buffer - checks for buffer cache hit rates for indexes and tables
- constraint - checks for invalid constraints
- all - runs all checks
You can optionally specify a single health check or a comma-separated list of health checks. The default is 'all' checks.
- ToolName: get_top_queries          Description: Reports the slowest or most resource-intensive queries using data from the 'pg_stat_statements' extension.
- ToolName: execute_sql              Description: Execute any SQL query

===== Execution Logs =====
| execute_sql {"sql": "-- Task 1: Identify Data Inconsistencies\nSELECT ls.set_num, ls.num_parts AS stored_num_parts, COALESCE(actual_parts, 0) AS actual_parts\nFROM public.lego_sets ls\nLEFT JOIN (\n  SELECT li.set_num, SUM(lip.quantity) AS actual_parts\n  FROM public.lego_inventories li\n  JOIN public.lego_inventory_parts lip ON li.id = lip.inventory_id\n  WHERE lip.is_spare = false\n  AND (li.set_num, li.version) IN (\n    SELECT set_num, MAX(version) FROM public.lego_inventories GROUP BY set_num\n  )\n  GROUP BY li.set_num\n) latest_inventory_parts ON ls.set_num = latest_inventory_parts.set_num\nWHERE ls.num_parts <> COALESCE(actual_parts, 0);\n"}
| execute_sql {"sql": "-- Task 2 Step 1: Create a Temporary Table\nCREATE TEMP TABLE correct_counts (\n    set_num TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n    actual_parts INTEGER\n);\n\n-- Task 2 Step 2: Populate the Temporary Table\nINSERT INTO correct_counts (set_num, actual_parts)\nSELECT ls.set_num, COALESCE(latest_parts.actual_parts, 0) AS actual_parts\nFROM public.lego_sets ls\nLEFT JOIN (\n  SELECT li.set_num, SUM(lip.quantity) AS actual_parts\n  FROM public.lego_inventories li\n  JOIN public.lego_inventory_parts lip ON li.id = lip.inventory_id\n  WHERE lip.is_spare = false\n  AND (li.set_num, li.version) IN (\n    SELECT set_num, MAX(version) FROM public.lego_inventories GROUP BY set_num\n  )\n  GROUP BY li.set_num\n) latest_parts ON ls.set_num = latest_parts.set_num;\n\n-- Task 2 Step 3: Update the lego_sets num_parts from the temporary table\nUPDATE public.lego_sets ls\nSET num_parts = cc.actual_parts\nFROM correct_counts cc\nWHERE ls.set_num = cc.set_num;\n"}
| execute_sql {"sql": "-- Task 3 Part A: Create the trigger function\ndrop function if exists check_set_parts_consistency cascade;\n\nCREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION check_set_parts_consistency()\nRETURNS trigger\nLANGUAGE plpgsql\nAS $$\nDECLARE\n    relevant_set_num TEXT;\n    stored_num_parts INTEGER;\n    actual_parts INTEGER;\nBEGIN\n    -- Determine set_num based on triggering table\n    IF TG_TABLE_NAME = 'lego_sets' OR TG_TABLE_NAME = 'lego_inventories' THEN\n        relevant_set_num := NEW.set_num;\n    ELSIF TG_TABLE_NAME = 'lego_inventory_parts' THEN\n        SELECT set_num INTO relevant_set_num FROM lego_inventories WHERE id = NEW.inventory_id;\n        IF relevant_set_num IS NULL THEN\n            RAISE EXCEPTION 'Inventory id % has no associated set_num', NEW.inventory_id;\n        END IF;\n    ELSE\n        RAISE EXCEPTION 'Trigger fired on unexpected table: %', TG_TABLE_NAME;\n    END IF;\n\n    -- Get stored num_parts from lego_sets\n    SELECT num_parts INTO stored_num_parts FROM lego_sets WHERE set_num = relevant_set_num;\n    IF stored_num_parts IS NULL THEN\n        -- If no such set exists in lego_sets, skip check\n        RETURN NEW;\n    END IF;\n\n    -- Calculate actual parts from latest inventory non-spare parts\n    SELECT COALESCE(SUM(lip.quantity), 0) INTO actual_parts\n    FROM lego_inventories li\n    JOIN lego_inventory_parts lip ON li.id = lip.inventory_id\n    WHERE li.set_num = relevant_set_num\n    AND lip.is_spare = false\n    AND li.version = (\n        SELECT MAX(version) FROM lego_inventories WHERE set_num = relevant_set_num\n    );\n\n    -- Raise exception if inconsistency found\n    IF stored_num_parts <> actual_parts THEN\n        RAISE EXCEPTION 'Inconsistent part count for set %: stored = %, actual = %', relevant_set_num, stored_num_parts, actual_parts;\n    END IF;\n\n    RETURN NEW;\nEND;\n$$;\n\n-- Task 3 Part B: Create the constraint triggers\n\nDROP TRIGGER IF EXISTS trg_lego_sets_consistency ON public.lego_sets;\nCREATE CONSTRAINT TRIGGER trg_lego_sets_consistency\nAFTER INSERT OR UPDATE ON public.lego_sets\nDEFERRABLE INITIALLY IMMEDIATE\nFOR EACH ROW\nEXECUTE FUNCTION check_set_parts_consistency();\n\nDROP TRIGGER IF EXISTS trg_lego_inventories_consistency ON public.lego_inventories;\nCREATE CONSTRAINT TRIGGER trg_lego_inventories_consistency\nAFTER INSERT OR UPDATE ON public.lego_inventories\nDEFERRABLE INITIALLY IMMEDIATE\nFOR EACH ROW\nEXECUTE FUNCTION check_set_parts_consistency();\n\nDROP TRIGGER IF EXISTS trg_lego_inventory_parts_consistency ON public.lego_inventory_parts;\nCREATE CONSTRAINT TRIGGER trg_lego_inventory_parts_consistency\nAFTER INSERT OR UPDATE ON public.lego_inventory_parts\nDEFERRABLE INITIALLY IMMEDIATE\nFOR EACH ROW\nEXECUTE FUNCTION check_set_parts_consistency();\n"}
Task 1: The query to identify inconsistent sets was executed and returned multiple sets where the stored `num_parts` does not match the calculated parts from the latest inventory.

Task 2: The process to fix inconsistencies was executed by creating a temporary table, populating it with correct part counts for all sets, and updating the `lego_sets` table accordingly. This completed successfully.

Task 3: A deferrable constraint trigger system was implemented:
- Created the PL/pgSQL trigger function `check_set_parts_consistency()` that enforces the part count consistency rule.
- Created deferrable, initially immediate constraint triggers on `lego_sets`, `lego_inventories`, and `lego_inventory_parts` tables that invoke this function after inserts or updates, ensuring future data consistency.

Task completed.
